From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:24:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "tracing: perf: Fix stale head for perf syscall
 tracing"

This reverts commit 501235c883b34, the backport of upstream commit
2c2b322acdcc78575b8d6afa64a085cf92e03c12, which Ubuntu took from the
7.1.y stable series.

Upstream moved the BPF program call in perf_syscall_enter() before the
per-CPU perf event check with commit 57918341dd19 ("bpf: Add sleepable
support for classic tracepoint programs") in v7.2. The backported fix
relies on that order: it returns early when the perf event list of the
current CPU is empty.

v7.0 still runs BPF programs after that point, so the early return
skips BPF programs attached to sys_enter tracepoints of syscalls with
user space pointer arguments on every CPU without its own perf event,
for example execve and openat. Tools that attach such programs through
a single perf event then see these syscalls only on one CPU.

The stale head issue the backport fixes does not exist in v7.0, where
perf_syscall_enter() reads the per-CPU head after the code that may
migrate.

Link: https://bugzilla.proxmox.com/show_bug.cgi?id=8332
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 kernel/trace/trace_syscalls.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/trace/trace_syscalls.c b/kernel/trace/trace_syscalls.c
index ea6946d4c81abe22472e304ebd1b47c9a3f482fd..64b60e1d18eeb72660b3cd05f74eaf35c8315d6a 100644
--- a/kernel/trace/trace_syscalls.c
+++ b/kernel/trace/trace_syscalls.c
@@ -1437,11 +1437,6 @@ static void perf_syscall_enter(void *ignore, struct pt_regs *regs, long id)
 		if (syscall_get_data(sys_data, args, &user_ptr,
 				     &size, user_sizes, &uargs, buf_size) < 0)
 			return;
-
-		/* The above may have caused a migration */
-		head = this_cpu_ptr(sys_data->enter_event->perf_events);
-		if (hlist_empty(head))
-			return;
 	}
 
 	head = this_cpu_ptr(sys_data->enter_event->perf_events);
